# Backend Services

Per-service detail: `apps/<service>/AGENTS.md`. Shared rules:

- **Frameworks are fixed:** product-service & auth-service = Express 5; order-service, search-service, catalog-service, user-service, review-service, wishlist-service, tax-service, pricing-service, seller-service & commission-service = Fastify 5; payment-service, inventory-service & promotion-service = Hono; vendor-service = NestJS 10 (Fastify); payout-service & support-service = NestJS 11 (Fastify); fraud-service = Python 3.14 (FastAPI); email-service = headless Kafka worker. Do not introduce a different framework.
- **ESM:** `"type": "module"`. Local imports follow existing convention (explicit `.js` extensions).
- **Auth middleware first.** Use `shouldBeUser` / `shouldBeAdmin`; return `401` when
  unauthenticated and `403` when not an admin. Never leave a mutating route unguarded.
- **Data access via packages or Drizzle:** `@repo/product-db`, `@repo/inventory-db`, `@repo/user-db`, `@repo/vendor-db`, `@repo/support-db` (Prisma) or `@repo/order-db`, `@repo/cart-db` (Mongoose), or Drizzle ORM. Never create ad-hoc database clients or access another service's database.
- **Events via `@repo/kafka` only**, using the `{ value: payload }` envelope. Handlers
  must catch and log errors so the consumer keeps running.
- **Env from `process.env`**, documented in the workspace `.env.example`. No hardcoded
  secrets or connection strings (local Kafka broker list is in `@repo/kafka`).
- Add/update the topic contract in `docs/EVENT-DRIVEN-ARCHITECTURE.md` and in
  `@repo/types` when payloads change.
- **Mandatory 6-Pillar Feature Service Delivery Standard:**
  Whenever creating, expanding, or modifying any feature service, agents must strictly follow all 6 pillars:
  1. Front-End Delivery (`apps/admin/*`, `apps/client/*`)
  2. Cross-Service & Gateway Integration (`apps/*` all services, API Gateway, Kafka pipelines)
  3. Documentation, Skills, Manifests & Configuration Updates (`*.md`, skills, `*.yml`, Docker, K8s, CI/CD)
  4. Deep Project Analysis & Comprehensive Testing (Unit, Integration, 100% pass rate, 0 type errors)
  5. Security Audit & Zero-Trust Hardening (OWASP API Top 10, constant-time secret check, RBAC, redaction)
  6. Global README.md & Root Architecture Sync

Run `pnpm --filter <service> check-types` before finishing.
